\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Downtown Manhattan Beach Business and Professional Association Executive Director Kelly Stroman invited the community to attend the Holiday Open House and Pier Lighting on Thursday, November 19, 2025, from 5:00 PM - 9:00 PM; thanked the Public Works and Parks and Recreation Departments for their support in making the event special; announced a Holiday Scavenger Hunt for children running from November 19 through November 30, 2025; and noted that complimentary Santa photos will be available at the event, courtesy of Beach Santa Steve and Karl Meyer Photography.\line\line Recreation Supervisor Michael Hudak invited the community to participate in the Manhattan Beach Pickleball Turkey Tournament at Manhattan Heights Park, taking place from November 28 through November 30, 2025.\line\line Library Manager Cassandra Sargent announced an all-ages bingo event on Saturday, November 22, 2025; and invited the community to attend a Pressed Flower Luminary Jars program on Tuesday, November 25, 2025.\cf1\b\i0\line\line\cf0\b0\i Waste Management Recycling Education Representative Bobby Bell announced that collection services scheduled for Thursday and Friday will be delayed by one day next week due to the Thanksgiving holiday; and reminded the community that disposing of batteries in the trash is strongly discouraged, as it can cause fires in collection trucks and lead to service interruptions.\line\line Councilmember Howorth reported that she attended the Manhattan Beach Downtown Business and Professional Association meeting last week as part of her City Council assignment; and shared that the Community Development Department provided a Project Pulse presentation.\line\line\pard Mayor Lesser announced that the next Coffee with the Mayor will be held at Metlox Plaza on Friday, December 5, 2025, from 9:00 AM to 10:00 AM.\cf2\i0\f1\par
